# Verdicts for packaging/linux-only/early-port-followups.py: a team commit taken early (first sha) and a
# later team commit that touches the same code and has not reached the release yet (second sha).
#
#   <port sha> <later sha> port|skip <reason>
#
# port = the release must carry the later commit before it ships (it repairs the early port, or the port
#        needs it). skip = it does not; say why. Read the later commit and its pull request, and check the
#        release's own code, before writing a verdict. Add lines; do not delete them: they are the record.

# --- Early ports on top of the 2026-10-19 sync (6c159ad53): stable 1.4.0.6062 to 1.4.0.6103 ---

# The case that made this list. 9f192b60e dropped the clause that let the attacked creature keep fighting,
# so lair-enemy fights (only the instigator is flagged fight_til_death) stopped after half a second.
# a0fb5a095 checks both sides' flag. Shipped late, in stable 1.4.0.6103.
9f192b60e395 a0fb5a09552e port fixes the lair-enemy fights 9f192b60e broke (measured: 0 s vs 10 s with it)

f5bcdf10e468 da038f03ab5f skip UserState refactor (controlled thing moves to UserState); a refactor on others stable lacks, no fix to the possession camera
f5bcdf10e468 dc24c25248ce skip palette/lens state redesign onto LocalState/UserState (needs the UserState refactors); fixes no bug of the possession camera port
f5bcdf10e468 7fb7c94635d8 skip clean-up of user/player usage; a refactor
ddd6fccc82a8 92b0e7cd936b skip UserState refactor part 5 (instances); a refactor
ddd6fccc82a8 9a0b886e7134 skip spectator camera offset and lights: an older spectator issue, not caused by the rewind map/event-box fix
ddd6fccc82a8 0e8626c7821c skip disables rewind without kernel page tracking; deliberately not taken, this edition keeps the fallback
ddd6fccc82a8 dc24c25248ce skip palette/lens state redesign (needs the UserState refactors); not a repair of the rewind fix
ddd6fccc82a8 29b5eb6bcebe skip feature: rejoining a multiplayer game after a lost connection
ddd6fccc82a8 7fb7c94635d8 skip clean-up of user/player usage; a refactor
ddd6fccc82a8 4c0bc0a838d3 skip feature: Lua campaign data in saves
b520ee28cd83 1092314d2491 skip feature: defeated players become spectators
b520ee28cd83 d4c0f7ebd473 skip feature: the redesigned multiplayer lobby
52baf4ebb554 4c0bc0a838d3 skip feature: Lua campaign data in saves
52baf4ebb554 adfd6d4e77c7 skip feature: game-file check against the host; its Lua loads must go through this edition's sandbox before it is taken
52baf4ebb554 f4bad330f827 skip shares only apply_game_kfxs, and none of the map-config fix's lines: drops two panel refreshes reinit_level_after_load repeats after every load, and adds the config overlay to resync data. That fixes a desync stable also has (a resync keeps the client's own config), not the early port

# --- Early ports of 2026-11-06 (#5587, #5588): stable 1.4.0.6103 and alpha ahead of their sync ---

# f75ddc07b (#5581) lets several users share one keeper ("Hellhound mode", a testing feature). Each shared
# function only changes for that; none of the early ports' own lines change.
1b8545219ed0 f75ddc07b5c5 skip only power_hand_is_empty(player) -> (get_local_user()): the hand moves to each user; the pickup-priority fix's lines are untouched
f5bcdf10e468 f75ddc07b5c5 skip multi-user only: refuses a creature another user already possesses, handles a slap from another user during the zoom-in, set_player_lens -> set_user_lens; no change to the possession camera fix
8ea409b1ce23 f75ddc07b5c5 skip init_player_cameras moves its body into init_user_dungeon_camera unchanged, and a rejoining user resets only its own camera; the chicken-peck fix (update_first_person_position) is untouched
